### Requests for the IntelliJ HTTP client. Start the app first (dev profile, see README).
### Run each block with the green arrow next to it.

@host = http://localhost:8080

# demo product ids (loaded by the dev profile)
@mealBox = 0190f3c0-0000-7000-8000-000000000101
@wrap = 0190f3c0-0000-7000-8000-000000000102
@latte = 0190f3c0-0000-7000-8000-000000000103
@water = 0190f3c0-0000-7000-8000-000000000104


### 1. Products and how many are in stock
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products


### 2. Place an order. {{$uuid}} makes a new Idempotency-Key every time, so each send is a new sale.
###    The id of the order is remembered for request 4.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Terminal-Id: KIOSK-07
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{wrap}}", "quantity": 2 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "INR" }
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}


### 3. A retry: the SAME key sent twice. Run both; you get the same order and number, and the stock goes down once.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Terminal-Id: KIOSK-07
Idempotency-Key: sale-demo-001

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{latte}}", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "INR" }
}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Terminal-Id: KIOSK-07
Idempotency-Key: sale-demo-001

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{latte}}", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "INR" }
}


### 4. Read the order from request 2 back
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}


### 5. What the kitchen screen sees (orders with food to prepare appear within about a second)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/kitchen/tickets


### 6. A card payment must be exactly the total. Wrap x2 = 396.90
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{wrap}}", "quantity": 2 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CARD", "amount": "396.90", "currency": "INR" }
}


### ---------- things that should fail, to see the error bodies ----------

### 7. Not enough stock: 409 OUT_OF_STOCK (the meal box has only 10)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{mealBox}}", "quantity": 11 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "5000", "currency": "INR" }
}


### 8. Not enough cash: 422 PAYMENT_REJECTED
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{wrap}}", "quantity": 2 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "10", "currency": "INR" }
}


### 9. Paying in another currency: 422 CURRENCY_MISMATCH
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{wrap}}", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "USD" }
}


### 10. Unknown product: 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000999", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "INR" }
}


### 11. Quantity out of range: 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{wrap}}", "quantity": 9999 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "INR" }
}


### 12. No Idempotency-Key header: 400 MISSING_HEADER
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "{{wrap}}", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "payment": { "method": "CASH", "amount": "500", "currency": "INR" }
}


### 13. Not JSON at all: 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

this is not json
